## Original Content
'ऑपरेशन सिंदूर' के दौरान भारत ने पाकिस्तान के सरगोधा में किराना हिल्स या किसी परमाणु ठिकाने पर हमला नहीं किया था. इसका खुलासा पूर्व चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ जनरल अनिल चौहान ने किया है. उन्होंने बताया कि भारत का ड्रोन मिशन टारगेट न मिलने के कारण किराना हिल्स की पहाड़ियों से टकरा गया था, जिसकी वजह से हिल्स से धुआं उठा होगा.

## Summary
Former Chief of Defence Staff General Anil Chauhan clarified that India did not attack Kirana Hills or nuclear facilities in Pakistan during 'Operation Sindoor'. The smoke observed was due to a drone mission crashing after failing to find its target, not a deliberate strike. This debunks rumors of a military attack on a nuclear site.

## Key Points
- No Indian attack occurred on Kirana Hills or Sargodha nuclear facilities during 'Operation Sindoor'.
- A drone mission crashed into Kirana Hills due to failure in locating the target, causing smoke.
- General Anil Chauhan, former CDS, revealed the truth behind the incident.
- The incident was an accidental crash, not a planned military strike.
- Allegations of attacking a nuclear facility were unfounded.


